^bo2.6 Application Interface Protocol^bo

The application interface protocol adheres to the guidelines for server application message passing. All messages have a common header:
^ep
	+--------------------+--------------------+
	|    functionCode    |      toBeFreed     |
	+--------------------+--------------------+
	|                                         |
	+---             Reserved (0)          ---+
	|                                         |
	+-----------------------------------------+
	|                 SourcePID               |
	+-----------------------------------------+
	|                  DestPID                |
	+-----------------------------------------+
	|          Network Management Class       |
	+-----------------------------------------+
	|             Note = Command Code         |
	+-----------------------------------------+
	|                  Length                 |
	+-----------------------------------------+
	|   Control Byte     |   New Credits      |
	+--------------------+--------------------+
	|                  Status                 |
	+-----------------------------------------+
	|                                         |
	+---            Parameter Field        ---+
	|                                         |


The Network Management Class is TBD. Every command has a response, and the response has the same header format as the request. The command code field in the response message is the same as the command code field in the request, except that the highest order bit will be set to 1. The fields Control Byte, New Credits, and Status are part of the credit management layer. Function code is always zero.

^boAllocate Link command^bo

