^boGet Card Status command^bo

The command code is 5. The command format is:

	+-----------------------------------------+
	|              Property Length            |
	+-----------------------------------------+
	|                                         |
	+---             Properties            ---+
	|                                         |

The only property in the request is card number. The response format is:

	+-----------------------------------------+
	|                 Error                   |
	+--------------------+--------------------+
	|     Line0Used      |    Line1Used       |
	+--------------------+--------------------+
	|     Line2Used      |    Line3Used       |
	+--------------------+--------------------+

Line0Used, Line1Used, Line2Used, and Line3Used are booleans that indicate whether lines 0, 1, 2, and 3, respectively, are used for networking or not. A value of 'TRUE' indicates that the line is used by GRiD Network. See 2.5.6.

^bo2.7 Application Interface Usage^bo

Normal applications needing network services don't need to invoke the application interface at all. The procedures VfsSignOn, NetSignOn, VfsSignOff, and NetSignOff (described in the VIPC specification) that are supplied to the user allocate and free network links as necessary. Mail applications may wish to query Network Manager for GRiD Server names. Other special applications may need to know about network links and their properties, card status, etc.

A connection to Network Manager is not necessary in order to make queries. The application looks up Network Manager's process id in the name device, and sends in the request. Network Manager sends the response to the process identified by the 'SourcePid' field in the request.

^bo2.8 System Manager Interface (*)^bo

The system manager interface is not supported in the first release.
